---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import SEO from "@/components/SEO.astro";
import Sidebar from "@/components/Sidebar.astro";
import Stack from "@/components/Stack.astro";
import TableOfContents from "@/components/TableOfContents.astro";
import LazyThemedImage from "@/components/LazyThemedImage.astro";
import type { TocItem } from "@/lib/toc";
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";
import avatar from "@/images/avatar_1.webp";
import signature from "@/images/signature.webp";
import signatureDark from "@/images/signature-dark.webp";

const canonicalURL = new URL("/about", Astro.site).href;

const weight = (await getCollection("weight"))[0]?.data;
const lastWeighIn = weight?.entries.at(-1);
const goal = weight?.projection?.goal;

const toc: TocItem[] = [
  { slug: "looked-fine", text: "The life that looked fine from the outside", children: [] },
  { slug: "detroit", text: "Detroit", children: [] },
  { slug: "changing", text: "The job I fought for is changing", children: [] },
  { slug: "now", text: "Now", children: [] },
];

const sectionHeading =
  "text-2xl! leading-7! tablet:text-3xl! tablet:leading-8.5! font-medium pb-6";
---

<Layout>
  <SEO
    slot="head"
    title="About - Daniel Noworyta"
    description="Ten years in automotive, two and a half years of 4:30 alarms, a first dev job in 2020. Now the job is changing under me and I am writing about it from inside."
    canonicalURL={canonicalURL}
    type="website"
    person
  />
  <div class="px-(--inline-padding)">
    <Sidebar
      class={cn(
        "mx-auto max-w-4xl",
        "tablet:[--sidebar-width:var(--container-2xl)]",
        "tablet:[--sidebar-content-min:100px]",
        "tablet:[--sidebar-gap:4rem]",
      )}
    >
      <!-- CONTENT -->
      <div class="max-w-2xl">
        <h1
          id="introduction"
          class="bg-brand-gradient bg-clip-text text-transparent font-medium laptop:pb-12 mt-10"
        >
          Still in it.
        </h1>
        <div class="laptop:hidden relative py-4 border-y border-orange-600 mt-4">
          <TableOfContents toc={toc} />
        </div>
        <p class="pb-6 mt-4 laptop:mt-0 text-lg text-pretty">
          I'm Daniel. I write code for a living, which is a sentence I waited
          most of my adult life to say. This page is the long version of how
          that happened, and what it looks like now that the job is changing
          under me.
        </p>
        <Sidebar sidebarWidth="312px" class="mb-10 tablet:[--sidebar-gap:1rem]">
          <div>
            <Image
              loading="eager"
              src={avatar}
              alt="Daniel Noworyta"
              class="aspect-square w-full mx-auto rounded-lg block"
            />
          </div>
          <Stack
            space="calc(var(--spacing) * 4)"
            class="text-pretty [@media(min-width:702px)]:text-gray-1200 italic [@media(min-width:702px)]:pt-4"
          >
            <p>
              Full-stack developer, self-taught, working from home in Poland
              for a German company.
            </p>
            <p>Father of one. Weekend footballer, slower than I used to be.</p>
            <p class="[@media(min-width:702px)]:pb-4">
              I like dark mode, side projects, and pizza, in that order on a
              bad day.
            </p>
          </Stack>
        </Sidebar>

        <h2 id="looked-fine" class={sectionHeading}>
          The life that looked fine from the outside
        </h2>
        <Stack class="pb-10">
          <p>
            For ten years I was a Class A surface modeler in automotive. If you
            have ever run your hand along a car door and felt nothing catch,
            that was someone like me, staring at curvature plots in software
            most people have never heard of. Up at six, at the desk eight to
            five, and on a plane more often than not. Detroit, Turin, Sweden,
            Germany. On paper it was a good career. I had also hit the ceiling
            of it, and I knew it.
          </p>
          <p>
            The thing I actually wanted was on the other side of the same
            screen. I read tech blogs at night. I watched people build web
            pages on YouTube and thought, I could do that. Then I closed the
            laptop and got up at six again. For years.
          </p>
        </Stack>

        <h2 id="detroit" class={sectionHeading}>Detroit</h2>
        <Stack class="pb-10">
          <p>
            My son was born, and my company sent me to Detroit for six months.
            I missed the part of his life you don't get back. I am not going
            to dress that up. It was the lowest I have been, and it was also
            the moment the fear of failing finally weighed less than the fear
            of staying.
          </p>
          <p>
            I started with Udemy and YouTube. HTML, CSS, JavaScript. The alarm
            moved to 5:30, then 4:30, so I could study before the
            eight-to-five, and I coded again after my son was asleep. I redid
            the same courses two and three times because nobody was there to
            tell me what I was missing. Imposter syndrome is a polite name for
            it. Two and a half years of that, and in December 2020 someone paid
            me to write TypeScript for the first time.
          </p>
        </Stack>

        <h2 id="changing" class={sectionHeading}>
          The job I fought for is changing
        </h2>
        <Stack class="pb-10">
          <p>
            Since 2024 I've been at Vaillant, building the web and mobile app
            that heat pump installers use, in React and React Native. I work
            from home in Poland. I see my son every day. On the surface, this
            is the ending.
          </p>
          <p>
            It is not the ending, because the craft I gave a decade of mornings
            for is being rewritten while I hold it. I built a full-stack
            finance tracker with AI in an afternoon that would have taken me
            weeks in 2020. I love handcrafted code, and I can no longer pretend
            we have time for it. I don't know what a self-taught path into this
            industry looks like in three years. I don't know whether the ladder
            I climbed still exists. I don't have easy answers, and I'm not
            going to invent them for a nicer paragraph.
          </p>
        </Stack>

        <h2 id="now" class={sectionHeading}>Now</h2>
        <Stack class="pb-10">
          <p>What I'm doing about it, in public.</p>
          <ul class="stack list-disc pl-5" style="--stack-space: 0.75rem">
            <li>
              Building <a href="https://github.com/Dan86de/opti" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline underline-offset-4 decoration-orange-500 hover:text-orange-500 transition-colors">OPTI</a>, my own MCP server, and a content CLI on top of it, so the
              AI I write with knows my voice and my backlog instead of guessing.
            </li>
            <li>
              One email a week about what I built with AI, what broke, and
              what I'm changing about how I work.
              <a href="/#newsletter" class="underline underline-offset-4 decoration-orange-500 hover:text-orange-500 transition-colors">Get the next one.</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              The same things on
              <a href="https://youtube.com/@danielnoworyta" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline underline-offset-4 decoration-orange-500 hover:text-orange-500 transition-colors">YouTube</a>,
              in English since this year, after years in Polish.
            </li>
            <li>
              My habits and my weight,
              <a href="/habits" class="underline underline-offset-4 decoration-orange-500 hover:text-orange-500 transition-colors">logged on this site</a>.
              {
                lastWeighIn && (
                  <>
                    <span class="tabular-nums">{lastWeighIn.value} {weight?.unit}</span>
                    {" "}today{goal ? `, aiming for ${goal}` : ""}.
                  </>
                )
              }
              A streak nobody can see is easy to drop.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            If you are where I was in 2018, reading this at midnight with an
            alarm set for six: the alarm is not the hard part. The hard part is
            the two and a half years where nothing visible happens. I'll show
            you what mine looked like.
          </p>
          <p>
            I still get to say I write code for a living. I'm just no longer
            sure what it will mean in three years, and I'd rather figure that
            out in public.
          </p>
        </Stack>

        <LazyThemedImage
          lightSrc={signature}
          darkSrc={signatureDark}
          width={300}
          alt="Signature"
          class="w-50 ml-auto"
        />
      </div>
      <!-- TOC -->
      <div class="hidden laptop:block mt-49 relative">
        <TableOfContents toc={toc} />
      </div>
    </Sidebar>
  </div>
</Layout>
